2. In this Order —
“CWA Singapore” means the company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50) as Cycling Without Age Singapore Ltd. (UEN 201714757N);
“specified e-trishaw” means a three‑wheeled pedal cycle that —
(a)is constructed or adapted for the carriage of passengers;
(b)is equipped with an electric motor;
(c)may be propelled by human power or by the electric motor with which it is equipped, or by both; and
(d)is used by CWA Singapore for the purpose of ferrying individuals;
“specified route” means a route, comprising one or more footpaths or shared paths, that is bounded or delineated by black‑coloured lines in the maps set out in the Schedule.
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]

3.—(1) Sections 16(1)(b) and 17(1) of the Act do not apply to an individual who drives a specified e‑trishaw on any specified route during the driving times and the days of the week mentioned in sub‑paragraph (2), under the following conditions:
(a)the individual has completed a training course conducted by CWA Singapore on how to drive the specified e‑trishaw;
(b)the individual is authorised by CWA Singapore to drive the specified e‑trishaw;
(c)the specified e-trishaw is only used to carry, for their leisure, passengers who belong to any class of passengers that is approved by the Authority to be carried on a specified e‑trishaw;
(d)the specified e‑trishaw is not used to carry passengers for hire or reward;
(e)the individual who drives the specified e‑trishaw —
(i)drives at a speed not exceeding 10 km/h;
(ii)does not carry, at any time, more than 2 passengers;
(iii)drives with all passengers on the specified e‑trishaw safely secured;
(iv)gives way to other users of the footpath or shared path;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(v)keeps a distance of at least 50 metres away from —
(A)any other specified e‑trishaw; or
(B) (where sub‑paragraph (vi) applies) any other group of specified e‑trishaws, or any other specified e‑trishaw that is not in a group of specified e‑trishaws; and
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(vi)drives the specified e‑trishaw on the specified route with other drivers of specified e‑trishaws in a group, only if —
(A)the specified route is in Part 15 of the Schedule; and
(B)the group of specified e‑trishaws consists of not more than 3 specified e‑trishaws;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(f)the specified e‑trishaw is accompanied by a safety marshal who ensures the safe use of the specified e‑trishaw;
(g)there is in force, at any time the specified e‑trishaw is used, a policy of insurance in relation to the specified e‑trishaw insuring against any liability in respect of the death of or bodily injury sustained by any person (other than the driver or any passenger of the specified e‑trishaw), or property damage suffered by any person (other than the driver or any passenger of the specified e‑trishaw), caused by or arising out of the use of the specified e‑trishaw;
(h)the risk under the policy of insurance mentioned in sub‑paragraph (g) is assumed by an insurer who, at the time of the issuance of the policy, is lawfully carrying on an insurance business in Singapore;
(i)no more than the number of specified e-trishaws mentioned in sub‑paragraph (3) are used at any time on the specified route.
(2) The driving times and days of the week are as follows:
(a)for the specified routes in Parts 1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 10, 11, 13, 14 and 16 of the Schedule — from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. on a weekday, Saturday or Sunday;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
[S 306/2026 wef 28/05/2026]
(b)for the specified route in Part 2 of the Schedule — from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. on a weekday, Saturday or Sunday;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
[S 621/2025 wef 27/09/2025]
(ba)[Deleted by S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(c)[Deleted by S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(d)for the specified route in Part 6 of the Schedule —
(i)from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. on a Saturday, Sunday or weekday (being a public holiday); and
(ii)from 9.30 a.m. to 5 p.m. on a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or weekday (being a public holiday);
[S 918/2024 wef 29/11/2024]
(da)for the specified routes in Parts 7 and 7A of the Schedule — from 9.30 a.m. to 5.30 p.m. on a weekday, Saturday or Sunday;
[S 418/2023 wef 24/06/2023]
[S 621/2025 wef 27/09/2025]
[S 306/2026 wef 28/05/2026]
(db)for the specified route in Map A7.3 in Part 7 of the Schedule — from 5.30 p.m. to 7 p.m. on 22 August 2026;
[S 567/2026 wef 22/08/2026]
(e)for the specified route in Part 9 of the Schedule —
(i)from 12 p.m. to 3 p.m. on a Saturday, Sunday or weekday (being a public holiday); and
(ii)from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. on a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or weekday (being a public holiday);
(f)[Deleted by S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(g)[Deleted by S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(h)for the specified route in Part 12 of the Schedule — from 10 a.m. to 4.30 p.m. on a weekday, Saturday or Sunday;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(i)for the specified route in Part 13A of the Schedule —
(i)from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. on a Saturday, Sunday or weekday (being a public holiday); and
(ii)from 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. on a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or weekday (being a public holiday);
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
[S 306/2026 wef 28/05/2026]
(j)for the specified route in Part 15 of the Schedule — from 9 a.m. to 12 noon and 2 p.m. to 4 p.m. on a weekday, Saturday or Sunday.
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(3) The number of specified e-trishaws allowed on each specified route are as follows:
(a)for the specified routes in Parts 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7A, 8, 13A, 14 and 16 of the Schedule — 4;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
[S 306/2026 wef 28/05/2026]
(aa)for the specified routes in Parts 7 and 12 of the Schedule — 2;
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
(b)for the specified route in Part 9 of the Schedule — 1;
(c)for the specified routes in Parts 10, 11, 13 and 15 of the Schedule — 6.
[S 229/2025 wef 31/03/2025]
